WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.072
When King Zhuang of Chu first took the throne, he spent all day only amusing himself.

00:00:03.422 --> 00:00:06.110
For a long time he did not attend to the affairs of state.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.932
He even ordered that whoever advised him would be punished.

00:00:09.282 --> 00:00:12.570
The ministers were very worried, yet dared not advise him directly.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.368
The affairs of Chu slowly piled up, unattended.

00:00:15.718 --> 00:00:19.390
The minister Wu Ju used the image of a great bird to remind King Zhuang.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.932
He said: there is a bird that for three years has neither flown nor cried out.

00:00:23.282 --> 00:00:26.402
Having spoken, Wu Ju waited nervously for the king's answer.

00:00:26.752 --> 00:00:30.424
King Zhuang smiled and answered: this bird, once it flies —

00:00:30.774 --> 00:00:35.262
— will soar straight to the sky; and once it cries out, it will amaze everyone.

00:00:35.612 --> 00:00:38.300
It turned out King Zhuang had been quietly observing everyone all along.

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:42.850
From then on, King Zhuang began to set state affairs in order.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.488
He employed worthy men, and Chu grew stronger and stronger.

00:00:46.838 --> 00:00:50.126
Those who performed badly were replaced; the capable were given important posts.

00:00:50.476 --> 00:00:53.764
King Zhuang later became a famous ruler of the Spring and Autumn period.

00:00:54.114 --> 00:00:57.354
"One cry amazes everyone" became a beloved idiom.

00:00:57.704 --> 00:01:01.112
Sometimes, the quiet one is preparing to fly even higher.

